+#### Spectrum analyzer commands
+
+CamillaDSP includes a built-in FFT spectrum analyzer. It runs in its own
+thread, taps the audio at the capture side (before the pipeline, the source)
+and the playback side (after the pipeline, the destination), and publishes
+averaged log-spaced levels for the whole spectrum at a fixed rate of 10 Hz.
+This is a replacement for the "filter bank" hack used by some tools, where a
+bank of bandpass filters was injected into the config to get similar data.
+
+The analyzer is disabled by default. While disabled, the cost is a single
+atomic load per audio chunk, and no memory is copied. When enabled the cost
+is small (of the order of one percent of a single CPU core on typical
+hardware), and can be reduced further with a smaller FFT size and a longer
+interval.
+
+- `GetSpectrumConfig` : read the current analyzer configuration.
+  Returns a json object with keys `enabled`, `fftsize`, `bins`, `smoothing`,
+  `capture_channel`, `playback_channel` and `interval_ms`.
+- `SetSpectrumEnabled` : enable or disable the analyzer. Takes a boolean.
+  Disabling also clears the published levels.
+- `GetSpectrumLevels` : read the current spectrum of both taps.
+  Returns a json object with keys `capture` and `playback`, each containing
+  an object with:
+  * `active`: false when no audio has been seen for the last second.
+  * `samplerate`: the sample rate the levels refer to.
+  * `fftsize`: the FFT length used, see `SetSpectrumFftSize`.
+  * `frequencies`: center frequency in Hz of each bin.
+  * `levels`: smoothed level of each bin in dBFS. A full-scale sine gives 0 dB.
+  
+  The bins are log-spaced over the whole spectrum, from the first FFT bin up
+  to Nyquist. Poll this command at the configured interval to get all updates.
+- `SetSpectrumChannel` : select which channel to analyze for a tap.
+  Takes the tap (`"capture"` or `"playback"`) and the channel index.
+  The channel is clamped to the number of channels actually available.
+  Capture channels are counted before the pipeline (the source channels),
+  playback channels after it (the destination channels).
+- `SetSpectrumBins` : change the number of log-spaced output bins.
+  Takes an integer in the range 8 to 256. Default is 31.
+- `SetSpectrumSmoothing` : change the exponential averaging of the levels.
+  Takes a float in the range 0.0 (no smoothing, instantaneous) to 0.99
+  (very slow). The averaging is done in dB domain, which gives a
+  display-friendly linear decay. Default is 0.7.
+- `SetSpectrumFftSize` : change the FFT length. One of 1024, 2048, 4096 or
+  8192. Smaller is cheaper but gives coarser frequency resolution.
+  Default is 2048, which gives about 23 Hz resolution at 48 kHz. Since the
+  display bins are much wider than that except at the lowest frequencies,
+  this is the recommended setting for a graphical equalizer display. On
+  very weak hardware, 1024 plus a longer interval brings the cost down
+  further.
+- `SetSpectrumInterval` : change the analyzer update interval in ms,
+  in the range 50 to 1000. Default is 100 (10 Hz).
+
 
 ### Volume control
 
